1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,820
My name is Maznah anak Unyan.
I was born on 18 March 1968

2
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:09,870
in Kampung Orang Asli Sungai Bumbun,
Carey Island, Kuala Langat, Selangor.

3
00:00:09,950 --> 00:00:12,650
### NEW SCRIPT — not in the old cut, needs writing ###

4
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:19,870
I started learning to weave
when I was 12 years old

5
00:00:19,950 --> 00:00:21,370
from my mother.

6
00:00:21,450 --> 00:00:27,300
When I grew up, this weaving
became my daily source of income.

7
00:00:27,550 --> 00:00:32,200
The materials we use all come
from around our village,

8
00:00:32,450 --> 00:00:37,000
on Carey Island: mengkuang, pandan
and also nipah leaves.

9
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:41,850
I did not want to stop
where my mother stopped.

10
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:45,750
I observed for myself,
and I tried to make weaving

11
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:49,350
that is neater and more orderly.

12
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:52,020
From there I created new products:

13
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:55,450
women's accessories, bookmarks,

14
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:58,720
and I created two origami pieces
from nipah leaves,

15
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:01,750
a dragonfly and a butterfly.

16
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,250
Before this, the products
of the Mah Meri people

17
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:10,250
only came in ordinary colours.

18
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:15,220
After I joined a workshop organised
by the Department of Agriculture

19
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:17,150
in Kampung Rusila, Terengganu,

20
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:22,320
Kraftangan Malaysia's
Selangor branch

21
00:01:22,400 --> 00:01:25,450
taught us how to dye,
and Gerai OA

22
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:29,850
taught us about the colours
that are popular with

23
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:34,650
customers who love pandan
and mengkuang weaving.

24
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,350
This learning will never stop.
Learn, and keep learning.

25
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:45,300
Since 2005,
I have also been the leader,

26
00:01:45,450 --> 00:01:52,000
gathering with my relatives,
my niece, mother and siblings.

27
00:01:52,450 --> 00:01:58,370
The ways of weaving all came from my mother.
I sought the roots from my mother.

28
00:01:58,450 --> 00:01:59,870
I learned and kept learning.

29
00:01:59,950 --> 00:02:03,570
After that, my niece and I
were worried

30
00:02:03,650 --> 00:02:06,150
because we were just one family.
What could we do?

31
00:02:06,250 --> 00:02:09,300
Then my niece
promoted it,

32
00:02:09,550 --> 00:02:14,200
meeting other relatives
at the clinic and at weddings.

33
00:02:14,550 --> 00:02:19,000
At that time, I was also teaching

34
00:02:19,450 --> 00:02:23,000
in my own village,
Kampung Orang Asli Sungai Bumbun,

35
00:02:23,550 --> 00:02:28,800
and also went to another village,
Kampung Orang Asli Sungai Judah,

36
00:02:28,950 --> 00:02:34,400
with Kraftangan Malaysia
to run a workshop there.

37
00:02:34,650 --> 00:02:38,200
At that time I was with my niece,
Junadah anak Karim,

38
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:42,670
and also, indirectly,
Kampung Orang Asli Sungai Kurau,

39
00:02:42,750 --> 00:02:45,900
### NEW SCRIPT — not in the old cut, needs writing ###

40
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:50,750
Tompoq Tompoh was founded in 2005.

41
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:55,820
Many Orang Asli women still do not dare
to face the outside world,

42
00:02:55,900 --> 00:02:58,850
let alone become entrepreneurs.

43
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:04,970
So I founded an association,
this Tompoq Tompoh,

44
00:03:05,050 --> 00:03:07,850
### NEW SCRIPT — not in the old cut, needs writing ###

45
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:12,650
This weaving has taken me

46
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:16,820
far from Malaysia, for example

47
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:23,650
to the Philippines, DAYAW 2017,
to Isabela in 2006,

48
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:27,420
to Vietnam in 2007,

49
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:32,220
to the International Festival of
Orang Asli and Indigenous Arts,

50
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:37,850
in 2023 to London Craft Week,

51
00:03:38,250 --> 00:03:42,400
and also to Expo 2025

52
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:47,150
Osaka, Kansai, Japan for 3 months.

53
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:51,620
The mengkuang plants that
my late mother planted,

54
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:57,850
I share with the weaving participants
in Kampung Orang Asli Sungai Bumbun,

55
00:03:58,300 --> 00:04:03,550
Kampung Orang Asli Sungai Judah and
Kampung Orang Asli Sungai Kurau.

56
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:07,350
Not only within Carey Island,

57
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:11,820
the seedlings have been spread widely
across Malaysia,

58
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:17,020
for example Kelantan, Perak and also Johor,
in Kampung Peta.

59
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:21,750
They go to the pandan and
mengkuang weaving participants,

60
00:04:21,900 --> 00:04:27,150
who take the seedlings
back to their own states.

61
00:04:28,150 --> 00:04:46,350
### NEW SCRIPT — not in the old cut, needs writing ###

62
00:04:47,100 --> 00:04:50,920
And in 2023,

63
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:55,850
I was recognised as the Adiguru Kraf
of Mah Meri weaving.

64
00:04:56,600 --> 00:05:08,400
